<title>UK: Czarnikow sees lower 96/97 Thai white sugar export.</title>
<headline>Czarnikow sees lower 96/97 Thai white sugar export.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's white sugar exports from this year's cane harvest are likely to reach 1.2 million tonnes tel quel, down from earlier forecasts of up to 1.35 million, Czarnikow Sugar said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But raw sugar exports were still expected to reach some 2.8 million tonnes despite the slow rate of shipments to date, it said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>In its February report, Czarnikow estimated Thailand's sugar production for 1996/97 at 6.42 million tonnes raw value, up from 6.32 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Czarnikow said some Thai mills were reported to have repurchased earlier contracts.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
